{"type":"npc","name":"Lightling","folder":"gtfya5QlMXbZtjD2","system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":77,"temp":0,"max":77,"details":""},"ac":{"value":22,"details":"(24 with lantern raised)"},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":15}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"blinded","exceptions":[]},{"type":"fire","exceptions":[]},{"type":"sleep","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","luxan","pyric","spirituan"],"details":""},"level":{"value":5},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Lightlings can be found in derelict dungeons, deep caverns, and any of the world's dark reaches. Here, their sole mission is to tend to torches, lanterns, and other guiding lights so that travelers lost in such darkness are not without hope of finding their way home.</p><p>Light is essential for preserving these spirits' corporeal forms. As such, they never stray far from their flock of lights without a magically empowered lantern clutched in hand. While it would seem safest to simply live aboveground, lightlings rarely seek the security of daylight or other natural light sources. While the reason for this decision is uncertain, some believe the choice to place themselves in constant peril is a means of self-discipline on the lightlings' part. Perhaps they prefer shedding their physical forms to the possibility of failure in their work.</p><p>Most lightlings are shy, skittish creatures, typically content to mind their own business so long as no one threatens the lights they tend. However, they sometimes take more active roles in their work, acting as personal guides to lost travelers or slaying creatures of darkness that dare to encroach on the lightlings' domains. Of course, even those who serve reactively as wardens often must contend with the other denizens of the underground who don't take kindly to the presence of all the lights.</p><hr /><p>Elemental spirits are spiritual beings who embody one or more elements, though those of composite elements tend to be more complex existences.</p><h2>You Going to Pay For That?</h2><p>While lightlings generally aren't belligerent, they often demand supplies or services as payment from those they believe they have aided. Lightlings' taciturn nature can make these demands difficult to interpret for the spiritually naïve. Poorly negotiated payments are a frequent source of irritation to the spirits and have been the cause of more than one traveler finding themselves suddenly lost in the darkness.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), skill items (Acrobatics, Crafting, Occultism, Survival, Thievery)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, burning barbs, dexterity, energy resistant (fire, vitality), fire, fire shield, intelligence, light, spirit, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Lachlan Carlsson-Forbes","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":2},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":3}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":13,"senses":[],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":12},"crafting":{"base":12},"occultism":{"base":11},"survival":{"base":13},"thievery":{"base":12}},"traits":{"value":["fire","spirit"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"_id":"aWNt1vaZ7VJK0P63","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/lightling.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lightling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"mod